{
  "video": {
    "id": "x_vlxGFrZLY",
    "title": "Transcription & Translation | MIT 7.01SC Fundamentals of Biology",
    "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x_vlxGFrZLY",
    "channel": "MIT OpenCourseWare",
    "duration": 583,
    "language": "en"
  },
  "segment_count": 134,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 6.93,
      "end": 7.9,
      "duration": 0.97,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Hi."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 7.9,
      "end": 11.18,
      "duration": 3.28,
      "text": "In this clip, we're going to go through problem two of the"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 11.18,
      "end": 13.67,
      "duration": 2.49,
      "text": "transcription and translation unit."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 13.67,
      "end": 16.39,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "We're also going to review all of the information you would"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 16.39,
      "end": 19.71,
      "duration": 3.32,
      "text": "need to fill out problem one, the table."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 19.71,
      "end": 22.28,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "If you haven't tried these problems yet on your own,"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 22.28,
      "end": 25.78,
      "duration": 3.5,
      "text": "please pause the video now and try them, and then come back"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 25.78,
      "end": 27.275,
      "duration": 1.495,
      "text": "and watch this explanation."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 30.0,
      "end": 30.84,
      "duration": 0.84,
      "text": "OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 30.84,
      "end": 36.74,
      "duration": 5.9,
      "text": "So here we have, as in problem two, the double stranded DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 36.74,
      "end": 41.05,
      "duration": 4.31,
      "text": "Now, this is a piece of the eukaryotic genome, and so this"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 41.05,
      "end": 44.05,
      "duration": 3.0,
      "text": "DNA is in the nucleus of the cell."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 44.05,
      "end": 47.08,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "Now what we're going to do is we're going to go through"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 47.08,
      "end": 50.97,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "transcription and translation with this gene."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 50.97,
      "end": 53.6,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "So the first thing we need to do is we need to figure out"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 53.6,
      "end": 56.86,
      "duration": 3.26,
      "text": "where we want to start transcription and in what"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 56.86,
      "end": 59.78,
      "duration": 2.92,
      "text": "direction we want to go and what strand we want to use as"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 59.78,
      "end": 61.9,
      "duration": 2.12,
      "text": "our template."
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 61.9,
      "end": 65.99,
      "duration": 4.09,
      "text": "So in the problem, we're given our promoter region and we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 65.99,
      "end": 69.12,
      "duration": 3.13,
      "text": "given that our transcription starts right here at this"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 69.12,
      "end": 72.1,
      "duration": 2.98,
      "text": "arrow and moves in this direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 72.1,
      "end": 74.66,
      "duration": 2.56,
      "text": "So we know where we're starting and what direction"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 74.66,
      "end": 76.0,
      "duration": 1.34,
      "text": "we're moving in."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 76.0,
      "end": 81.28,
      "duration": 5.28,
      "text": "All transcription will proceed reading a template in the"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 81.28,
      "end": 85.22,
      "duration": 3.94,
      "text": "three prime to five prime direction and will polymerize"
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 85.22,
      "end": 88.64,
      "duration": 3.42,
      "text": "the RNA made in the five prime to three prime direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 88.64,
      "end": 91.6,
      "duration": 2.96,
      "text": "So what we need to do now is figure out what strand is"
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 91.6,
      "end": 94.43,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "going in the three prime to five prime direction and the"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 94.43,
      "end": 97.17,
      "duration": 2.74,
      "text": "direction that we're going to be transcribed."
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 97.17,
      "end": 100.08,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "So that means that this strand, which is going from"
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 100.08,
      "end": 107.52,
      "duration": 7.44,
      "text": "three prime over here down to five prime at the end, this is"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 107.52,
      "end": 110.09,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "going to be our template strand."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 110.09,
      "end": 114.79,
      "duration": 4.7,
      "text": "So our template strand is going to be at the bottom."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 119.34,
      "end": 119.74,
      "duration": 0.4,
      "text": "OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 119.74,
      "end": 123.9,
      "duration": 4.16,
      "text": "So when our RNA polymerase starts, it's going to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 123.9,
      "end": 128.35,
      "duration": 4.45,
      "text": "reading this template strand and adding nucleic acid,"
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 128.35,
      "end": 137.33,
      "duration": 8.98,
      "text": "adding nucleotide triphosphates, or NTPs, one by"
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 137.33,
      "end": 140.36,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "one together to make the RNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 140.36,
      "end": 143.29,
      "duration": 2.93,
      "text": "Now it's going to add these together by adding a"
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 143.29,
      "end": 147.4,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "phosphodiester bond in between all of the monomers."
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 147.4,
      "end": 150.19,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "So we're going to start our transcription."
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 150.19,
      "end": 158.9,
      "duration": 8.71,
      "text": "And basically, what I need to do is just use the"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 158.9,
      "end": 163.19,
      "duration": 4.29,
      "text": "complimentary base pair to my template strand."
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 163.19,
      "end": 164.83,
      "duration": 1.64,
      "text": "So I'm going to write it out here."
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 196.23,
      "end": 199.07,
      "duration": 2.84,
      "text": "So I've done a lot of transcription here."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 199.07,
      "end": 201.64,
      "duration": 2.57,
      "text": "Now where am I going to stop my transcription?"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 201.64,
      "end": 204.14,
      "duration": 2.5,
      "text": "I'm not going to stop just randomly in"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 204.14,
      "end": 205.4,
      "duration": 1.26,
      "text": "the middle of nowhere."
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 205.4,
      "end": 208.13,
      "duration": 2.73,
      "text": "What my RNA polymerase is going to do is it's going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 208.13,
      "end": 212.24,
      "duration": 4.11,
      "text": "stop when it gets to the end of this terminator sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 212.24,
      "end": 215.34,
      "duration": 3.1,
      "text": "So I'm going to keep transcribing until I get to"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 215.34,
      "end": 216.63,
      "duration": 1.29,
      "text": "the end of my terminator here."
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 231.25,
      "end": 232.25,
      "duration": 1.0,
      "text": "OK."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 232.25,
      "end": 234.34,
      "duration": 2.09,
      "text": "So this is my RNA strand."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 234.34,
      "end": 238.29,
      "duration": 3.95,
      "text": "And as I said before, we're going to polymerize this mRNA"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 238.29,
      "end": 241.636,
      "duration": 3.346,
      "text": "in the five prime to three prime direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 247.11,
      "end": 249.17,
      "duration": 2.06,
      "text": "OK, we've got our mRNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 249.17,
      "end": 252.71,
      "duration": 3.54,
      "text": "Since this is a eukaryotic cell and the mRNA right now is"
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 252.71,
      "end": 255.83,
      "duration": 3.12,
      "text": "in the nucleus, what we need to do is transport it out of"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 255.83,
      "end": 258.47,
      "duration": 2.64,
      "text": "the nucleus and into the cytoplasm where it will be"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 258.47,
      "end": 261.97,
      "duration": 3.5,
      "text": "translated by a ribosome."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 261.97,
      "end": 265.19,
      "duration": 3.22,
      "text": "Now what the ribosome is going to do is it's going to take"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 265.19,
      "end": 270.71,
      "duration": 5.52,
      "text": "this mRNA, which is a message that encodes the sequence of"
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 270.71,
      "end": 273.84,
      "duration": 3.13,
      "text": "amino acids that we need to put together to make the"
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 273.84,
      "end": 277.46,
      "duration": 3.62,
      "text": "protein, and we're going to take this message and we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 65,
      "start": 277.46,
      "end": 281.36,
      "duration": 3.9,
      "text": "going to find a place to start translation."
    },
    {
      "index": 66,
      "start": 281.36,
      "end": 284.5,
      "duration": 3.14,
      "text": "So what the ribosome is going to do is it's going to start"
    },
    {
      "index": 67,
      "start": 284.5,
      "end": 287.37,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "at the five prime end of the template and read towards the"
    },
    {
      "index": 68,
      "start": 287.37,
      "end": 289.48,
      "duration": 2.11,
      "text": "three prime end of the template."
    },
    {
      "index": 69,
      "start": 289.48,
      "end": 293.69,
      "duration": 4.21,
      "text": "It's going to read until it gets to a start codon."
    },
    {
      "index": 70,
      "start": 293.69,
      "end": 297.98,
      "duration": 4.29,
      "text": "The start codon is AUG."
    },
    {
      "index": 71,
      "start": 297.98,
      "end": 304.0,
      "duration": 6.02,
      "text": "So this is where we're going to start, and AUG encodes"
    },
    {
      "index": 72,
      "start": 304.0,
      "end": 305.25,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "methionine."
    },
    {
      "index": 73,
      "start": 308.42,
      "end": 314.5,
      "duration": 6.08,
      "text": "We're then going to read in three base pair codons down"
    },
    {
      "index": 74,
      "start": 314.5,
      "end": 317.2,
      "duration": 2.7,
      "text": "from the five prime end of our template to the three prime"
    },
    {
      "index": 75,
      "start": 317.2,
      "end": 318.45,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "end of our template."
    },
    {
      "index": 76,
      "start": 321.02,
      "end": 325.76,
      "duration": 4.74,
      "text": "And so we're going to keep going in this translation"
    },
    {
      "index": 77,
      "start": 325.76,
      "end": 329.35,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "until we reach what's called a stop codon."
    },
    {
      "index": 78,
      "start": 329.35,
      "end": 331.35,
      "duration": 2.0,
      "text": "Now there are three stop codons."
    },
    {
      "index": 79,
      "start": 331.35,
      "end": 343.73,
      "duration": 12.38,
      "text": "Stop codons are UAA, UGA, and UAG."
    },
    {
      "index": 80,
      "start": 343.73,
      "end": 347.72,
      "duration": 3.99,
      "text": "So if when my ribosome finds any of these three codons in"
    },
    {
      "index": 81,
      "start": 347.72,
      "end": 351.26,
      "duration": 3.54,
      "text": "frame, it's going to stop."
    },
    {
      "index": 82,
      "start": 351.26,
      "end": 356.51,
      "duration": 5.25,
      "text": "So I get all the way down here before I hit a stop codon on"
    },
    {
      "index": 83,
      "start": 356.51,
      "end": 358.4,
      "duration": 1.89,
      "text": "this transcript."
    },
    {
      "index": 84,
      "start": 358.4,
      "end": 361.31,
      "duration": 2.91,
      "text": "So what my ribosome is going to be doing as it's reading"
    },
    {
      "index": 85,
      "start": 361.31,
      "end": 365.38,
      "duration": 4.07,
      "text": "these codons is it's going to insert amino acid by amino"
    },
    {
      "index": 86,
      "start": 365.38,
      "end": 369.62,
      "duration": 4.24,
      "text": "acid, pairing them together with a peptide bond."
    },
    {
      "index": 87,
      "start": 369.62,
      "end": 382.13,
      "duration": 12.51,
      "text": "So we've got methionine bonded to histidine, tyrosine,"
    },
    {
      "index": 88,
      "start": 382.13,
      "end": 390.25,
      "duration": 8.12,
      "text": "leucine, and so on and so forth."
    },
    {
      "index": 89,
      "start": 397.48,
      "end": 402.63,
      "duration": 5.15,
      "text": "OK, so this is the protein chain that's encoded by this"
    },
    {
      "index": 90,
      "start": 402.63,
      "end": 404.76,
      "duration": 2.13,
      "text": "gene in the DNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 91,
      "start": 404.76,
      "end": 411.12,
      "duration": 6.36,
      "text": "And in proteins, we always synthesize from the N terminus"
    },
    {
      "index": 92,
      "start": 411.12,
      "end": 412.485,
      "duration": 1.365,
      "text": "to the C terminus."
    },
    {
      "index": 93,
      "start": 415.25,
      "end": 419.67,
      "duration": 4.42,
      "text": "OK, so we've gone through both transcription and translation."
    },
    {
      "index": 94,
      "start": 419.67,
      "end": 422.54,
      "duration": 2.87,
      "text": "Now what we want to do is we want to take into account what"
    },
    {
      "index": 95,
      "start": 422.54,
      "end": 425.65,
      "duration": 3.11,
      "text": "would happen if we had a mutation in our sequence."
    },
    {
      "index": 96,
      "start": 425.65,
      "end": 429.99,
      "duration": 4.34,
      "text": "So in this case, in this problem, we're going to insert"
    },
    {
      "index": 97,
      "start": 429.99,
      "end": 431.82,
      "duration": 1.83,
      "text": "a base pair right here."
    },
    {
      "index": 98,
      "start": 431.82,
      "end": 436.16,
      "duration": 4.34,
      "text": "So we're going to insert an extra T here"
    },
    {
      "index": 99,
      "start": 436.16,
      "end": 440.05,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "and an extra A here."
    },
    {
      "index": 100,
      "start": 440.05,
      "end": 444.34,
      "duration": 4.29,
      "text": "Now, if this is happening in the DNA, when our DNA is"
    },
    {
      "index": 101,
      "start": 444.34,
      "end": 447.13,
      "duration": 2.79,
      "text": "transcribed to make our RNA, what's going to"
    },
    {
      "index": 102,
      "start": 447.13,
      "end": 449.61,
      "duration": 2.48,
      "text": "happen to the RNA?"
    },
    {
      "index": 103,
      "start": 449.61,
      "end": 453.81,
      "duration": 4.2,
      "text": "Well, we're going to also add the corresponding base into"
    },
    {
      "index": 104,
      "start": 453.81,
      "end": 459.23,
      "duration": 5.42,
      "text": "our RNA, so we're going to have an extra U here."
    },
    {
      "index": 105,
      "start": 461.74,
      "end": 466.95,
      "duration": 5.21,
      "text": "So in addition to only adding one nucleotide in our RNA,"
    },
    {
      "index": 106,
      "start": 466.95,
      "end": 469.98,
      "duration": 3.03,
      "text": "this is also going to throw off our frame that we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 107,
      "start": 469.98,
      "end": 476.32,
      "duration": 6.34,
      "text": "reading when our ribosome is reading our RNA."
    },
    {
      "index": 108,
      "start": 476.32,
      "end": 481.31,
      "duration": 4.99,
      "text": "So instead of the frame that we had previously, we're now"
    },
    {
      "index": 109,
      "start": 481.31,
      "end": 482.92,
      "duration": 1.61,
      "text": "going to have a new frame."
    },
    {
      "index": 110,
      "start": 482.92,
      "end": 486.68,
      "duration": 3.76,
      "text": "So it's going to start at the same start codon and then read"
    },
    {
      "index": 111,
      "start": 486.68,
      "end": 495.35,
      "duration": 8.67,
      "text": "this codon just as normal, but then this U will make UUA and"
    },
    {
      "index": 112,
      "start": 495.35,
      "end": 498.82,
      "duration": 3.47,
      "text": "then will read in codons of three from there."
    },
    {
      "index": 113,
      "start": 501.47,
      "end": 508.25,
      "duration": 6.78,
      "text": "So again, I need to translate until I hit a stop codon."
    },
    {
      "index": 114,
      "start": 508.25,
      "end": 511.89,
      "duration": 3.64,
      "text": "And so the stop codon is going to be different in this case,"
    },
    {
      "index": 115,
      "start": 511.89,
      "end": 514.5,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "because this stop codon is no longer in frame."
    },
    {
      "index": 116,
      "start": 514.5,
      "end": 517.28,
      "duration": 2.78,
      "text": "I need to find an in frame stop codon."
    },
    {
      "index": 117,
      "start": 517.28,
      "end": 520.98,
      "duration": 3.7,
      "text": "And the first stop codon that I hit is going to be this you"
    },
    {
      "index": 118,
      "start": 520.98,
      "end": 523.299,
      "duration": 2.319,
      "text": "UAG right here."
    },
    {
      "index": 119,
      "start": 523.299,
      "end": 531.01,
      "duration": 7.711,
      "text": "And so our new protein sequence is now going to be N"
    },
    {
      "index": 120,
      "start": 531.01,
      "end": 537.54,
      "duration": 6.53,
      "text": "terminus, and then the beginning is going to be very"
    },
    {
      "index": 121,
      "start": 537.54,
      "end": 543.24,
      "duration": 5.7,
      "text": "similar, and then our amino acids are going to be"
    },
    {
      "index": 122,
      "start": 543.24,
      "end": 545.28,
      "duration": 2.04,
      "text": "completely different because we're reading this in a"
    },
    {
      "index": 123,
      "start": 545.28,
      "end": 546.53,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "different frame."
    },
    {
      "index": 124,
      "start": 554.18,
      "end": 558.28,
      "duration": 4.1,
      "text": "OK, so we can see how this one mutation, addition of one base"
    },
    {
      "index": 125,
      "start": 558.28,
      "end": 561.61,
      "duration": 3.33,
      "text": "pair into our DNA, has caused us to create a completely"
    },
    {
      "index": 126,
